  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 9-Demethoxy-18-demethylgardneramine and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as this compound acts as a target for multiple compounds that are themselves targets of the complex. Specifically, the compound is involved in the target of ME-180, Alstolucine B, and Kaempferol 7-O-rutinoside, all of which are known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings indicate that 9-Demethoxy-18-demethylgardneramine may serve as a mediator in the signaling pathways involving this complex, potentially through its role as a target of multiple compounds that modulate the complex's activity. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust association, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for this compound in the regulation of EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
